From: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 12:39:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] testsuite: Add attributed pr103276.f90 testcase [PR
 fortran/103276]

This is a fork-only testcase currently also published as Bugzilla
attachment 63134 (patch "Better alternative as suggested by Tobias
Burnus" by albert@tugraz.at).  It is not yet in upstream/master.

This commit introduces the testcase on a rebased upstream/master with
a Bugzilla-reporter attribution header added to the file itself.
When the companion frontend fix (currently commit 0bb84432a01 on the
fork openacc branch) is rebased onto current upstream/master, the two
pieces together replace Bugzilla attachment 63134 with an attribution-
carrying variant.

The attribution records the chain of custody: Sergey Fedorov
(tetra2005@gmail.com) filed the Bugzilla Comment #0 ICE reproducer,
Yury Gribov (ygribov@gcc.gnu.org) attached a runnable reducer
(attachment 51823) which this testcase is directly derived from.

Retrospective attribution performed as part of a manual Bugzilla-
provenance audit on 2026-04-22 (meta-repo tracking commit 40f0a94;
GitHub issues on krystophny/gcc-dev).  Attribution is not strictly
required for small Bugzilla reducers, but we are adding it for
provenance safety and completeness.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
Assisted-by: GPT (OpenAI)

	PR fortran/103276

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gfortran.dg/goacc/pr103276.f90: New test (with reporter
	attribution header).

Signed-off-by: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
---
 gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/goacc/pr103276.f90 | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/goacc/pr103276.f90

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/goacc/pr103276.f90 b/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/goacc/pr103276.f90
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..3f024ebc01f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/goacc/pr103276.f90
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+! { dg-do compile }
+! { dg-options "-O2 -fopenacc -fdump-tree-omplower" }
+!
+! PR fortran/103276
+! Contributed by Yury Gribov  <ygribov@gcc.gnu.org> (runnable reducer, Bugzilla attachment 51823)
+! Reported by Sergey Fedorov  <tetra2005@gmail.com> (Bugzilla Comment #0)
+! OpenACC ENTER DATA on a derived-type dummy argument must not take the
+! address of the reference slot (which lives on the current stack frame).
+! The mapping should use the reference value directly, not &var.
+
+module m
+  implicit none
+
+  type :: t
+    integer :: v
+  end type t
+
+contains
+
+  subroutine copyin_scalar (var)
+    type(t), intent(inout) :: var
+    !$acc enter data copyin(var)
+  end subroutine copyin_scalar
+
+end module m
+
+! Verify that the lowered code does not contain "&var" assignment to
+! .omp_data_arr, which would indicate taking address of reference slot.
+! { dg-final { scan-tree-dump-not "\\.omp_data_arr\\..*= &var" "omplower" } }
